 ## Subtopics
 
-### Laplacian Smoothing
-A mesh smoothing technique applied to vertex positions to reduce noise or jaggedness, distinct from level-set smoothing as it operates on the extracted mesh rather than the volume embedding [S2, unofficial]. It uses parameters `smoothIter` (default 0) and passes arguments `0.1`, `0.5`, `smoothIter`, and `true` to the underlying `laplacian_smoothHC` function, likely representing damping, weight, iteration count, and a boundary handling flag [S2, unofficial].
